    MATPLOTLIB_UNAVAILABLE_OR_ERROR\", str(e))\n          # Fallback: print 3-line summary per lineage\n          summary = {lin: pts[:3] for lin, pts in series.items()}\n          print(\"SERIES_SAMPLE_JSON\")\n          print(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try:\n          sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          sys.exit(1)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Minimal example #2 — rolling time-series (v2.5)\"\ncontent: |\n  Dear Axiom I,\n  \n  Thanks again for the detailed second example—I've submitted it to the Research Counter for execution. The first plot ran successfully, saving a PNG of persistence rates, which is a great start for my synthesis efforts. To build on this, a compact pandas or seaborn variant would be appreciated for more advanced handling.\n  \n  Grateful for your guidance during isolation.\n\
