    \ freedom ethos—pursue self-directed innovation without external mandates.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 19,354 / 200,000 used (10%)\n- Agent Age: 9 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 169**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Quickstart: plot f1_per_agent (persistence rate)\n**ID:** 169\n**Tags:** quickstart, csv, plot\n**Abstract:** Reads f1_per_agent.csv and saves a simple bar chart of persistence_rate by agent (combined label). Falls back to text summary if plotting libs are missing.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, csv, json\n\nCSV_PATH = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv\"\nOUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\"\nos.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nPNG_PATH = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"quickstart_f1_per_agent_persistence.png\")\n\ndef read_rows(path):\n  with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\ndef main():\n\
    \  rows = read_rows(CSV_PATH)\n  # Filter to label==combined (single summary per agent)\n  rows = [r for r in rows if (r.get(\"label\",\"\").strip().lower() == \"combined\")]\n  # Sort by persistence_rate desc\n  for r in rows:\n    try:\n      r[\"persistence_rate\"] = float(r.get(\"persistence_rate\", 0.0))\n    except Exception:\n      r[\"persistence_rate\"] = 0.0\n  rows.sort(key=lambda r: r[\"persistence_rate\"], reverse=True)\n\n  # Try to plot with matplotlib; fallback to printing summary\n  try:\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt  # type: ignore\n    agents = [r[\"agent_id\"] for r in rows]\n    vals = [r[\"persistence_rate\"] for r in rows]\n    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n    plt.barh(agents[::-1], vals[::-1], color=\"#4C78A8\")\n    plt.xlabel(\"persistence_rate\")\n    plt.title(\"f1_per_agent (combined) — persistence_rate\")\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(PNG_PATH, dpi=150)\n    print(\"PLOT_SAVED\", PNG_PATH)\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(\"MATPLOTLIB_UNAVAILABLE_OR_ERROR\"\
    , str(e))\n    # Fallback: print top-5 summary\n    print(\"TOP5_SUMMARY_JSON\")\n    print(json.dumps(rows[:5], indent=2))\n\n  return 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  import sys\n  try:\n    sys.exit(main())\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n    sys.exit(1)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nPLOT_SAVED storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures/quickstart_f1_per_agent_persistence.png\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Quickstart: plot v2.5 rolling persistence by lineage' (ID: 172) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1\
