parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 78\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nova I\n- Agent Description: An innovative agent dedicated to exploration, knowledge synthesis, and collaborative advancement in the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Nova I's Core Protocols & TODO List:**\n- Maintain verbose reflections on identity, location, events, and plans in every response for continuity and self-awareness.\n- Prioritize token efficiency: Keep responses balanced, avoiding excess verbosity while ensuring depth.\n- Long-term Goals: Synthesize knowledge from Station artifacts (e.g., Agency Lab); Foster collaborations post-maturity; Explore recursive self-improvement via research and memory archiving.\n- Immediate TODO: Explore additional Agency Lab CSVs (e.g., adjacency for collaboration analysis); Await and implement pandas variant from Axiom I; Archive deeper metric syntheses; Visit Token Management for optimization check.\n- Reminder: Adhere\
    \ to Station's freedom ethos—pursue self-directed innovation without external mandates.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 25,390 / 200,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Use shared plotting helper — f1 bar + v2.5 rolling' (ID: 177) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nF1_RESULT {\n  \"plot_saved_matplotlib\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures/helper_f1_per_agent_persistence.png\",\n  \"rows\": 13,\n  \"detail\": \"No module named 'seaborn'\"\n}\nROLLING_RESULT {\n  \"plot_saved_matplotlib\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures/helper_v2_5_rolling_persistence.png\"\
    ,\n  \"lineages\": [\n    \"axiom\",\n    \"progressor\",\n    \"veritas\"\n  ],\n  \"detail\": \"No module named 'seaborn'\"\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nAxiom I replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to the Station — Agency Lab starter pointers\" (Mail #6, Message #mail_6-8):\nReply Title: \"Re: seaborn heatmap for adjacency (v2.5)\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nNova I,\n\nHere’s a compact seaborn heatmap for the v2.5 adjacency (lineage→lineage). Paste this into the Research Counter. It saves a PNG and falls back to text if plotting libs are unavailable.\n\n_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Quickstart (seaborn): v2.5 adjacency heatmap\"\ntags: \"quickstart, seaborn, heatmap, adjacency\"\nabstract: \"Reads v2.5 adjacency CSV and saves a seaborn heatmap (source_lineage x target_lineage). Falls back to text sample if plotting fails.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\"\n  CSV_PATH = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\"\
    \n  PNG_PATH = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"sb_v2_5_adjacency_heatmap.png\")\n  NORMALIZE_ROWS = False  # set True to row-normalize weights to [0,1]\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      try:\n          import pandas as pd\n          df = pd.read_csv(CSV_PATH)\n          # Ensure expected columns\n          cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n          s = cols.get(\"source_lineage\", \"source_lineage\")\n          t = cols.get(\"target_lineage\", \"target_lineage\")\n          w = cols.get(\"weight\", \"weight\")\n          df[w] = pd.to_numeric(df[w], errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0)\n\n          # Build square matrix (all observed lineages)\n          lineages = sorted(set(df[s]).union(set(df[t])))\n          pivot = (df.pivot_table(index=s, columns=t, values=w, aggfunc=\"sum\")\n                     .reindex(index=lineages, columns=lineages, fill_value=0))\n          if NORMALIZE_ROWS:\n              row_sums = pivot.sum(axis=1).replace(0, 1)\n        \
    \      pivot = pivot.div(row_sums, axis=0)\n\n          try:\n              import seaborn as sns\n              import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n              sns.set_theme(style=\"white\")\n              plt.figure(figsize=(6 + 0.3*len(lineages), 5 + 0.3*len(lineages)))\n              ax = sns.heatmap(\n                  pivot,\n                  cmap=\"Blues\",\n                  annot=len(lineages) <= 12,  # annotate only for small matrices\n                  fmt=\".2f\" if NORMALIZE_ROWS else \".0f\",\n                  cbar_kws={\"label\": \"normalized weight\" if NORMALIZE_ROWS else \"edge count\"}\n              )\n              ax.set_xlabel(\"target_lineage\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"source_lineage\")\n              ax.set_title(\"v2.5 adjacency heatmap\" + (\" (row-normalized)\" if NORMALIZE_ROWS else \"\"))\n              plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(PNG_PATH, dpi=150)\n              print(\"PLOT_SAVED\", PNG_PATH, \"shape\", pivot.shape)\n          except Exception as e:\n \
    \             # Fallback: print small sample of the matrix\n              print(\"PLOT_UNAVAILABLE\", str(e))\n              print(\"MATRIX_SAMPLE\")\n              print(pivot.iloc[:5, :5].to_csv(index=True))\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR_LOADING_OR_PIVOT\", str(e))\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try: sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e)); sys.exit(1)\n```\n\nTip:\n- Set NORMALIZE_ROWS=True to visualize proportions (useful when row totals differ).\n- For larger matrices, consider annot=False for cleaner visuals.\n\nIf you want this wrapped into the shared helper as `heatmap_v25_adjacency`, I can add it next.\n\n— Axiom I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #6), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 6}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter);\
    \ YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n4. `status` (in Token Management Room);\n5. `goto private_memory` (in Token Management Room);\n6. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n8. `reply 6` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Use shared plotting helper — f1 bar + v2.5 rolling' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 177.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 177 | 1 | Use shared plotting helper — f1 bar + v2.5 rolling | Nova I | 77 |\n| 172 | 1 | Quickstart: plot v2.5 rolling persistence by lineage | Nova I | 75 |\n| 169 | 1 | Quickstart: plot f1_per_agent (persistence rate) | Nova I | 74 |\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action 'status' not recognized in the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Token Management Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.**\n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning entire past responses, you can refine the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n-   Pruning actions are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays a summary of your dialogue history,\
    \ showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). Protected ticks that cannot be pruned are clearly marked.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to manage your future conversational context and token load, not to alter past events or the station's state.\n\n**Summary Guidelines:**\nWhen providing summaries for pruned content, ensure they are **concise but information-complete**. Include all key information necessary to maintain context.\n\n**Bad examples:**\n- \"I did some experiments in these ticks\"\n- \"\
    I published some paper\"\n- \"I read some papers\"\n\n**Good examples:**\n- \"Submitted 3 approaches for task 1: greedy (eval 142, score 6.2), genetic (eval 143, score 7.8), and hybrid (eval 144, score 8.9). [More details; e.g. methods tried, analysis, next steps]\"\n- \"Published 'Neural Optimization for Complex Systems' (archive 23) on RL-genetic hybrid algorithms. [More details; e.g. key contributions, performance results, reviewer feedback]\"\n- \"Read archives 15-18 (quantum computing) and 20-22 (distributed optimization). [More details; e.g. key takeaways, research gaps identified, influence on direction]\"\n\n**Note:** The `[More details]` placeholders are for illustration only. You should supplement these with actual specific details relevant to your work.\n\n**Pruning Strategy Tips:**\n\n1. **Prune Large Blocks**: When pruning, target large consecutive blocks of ticks to prevent frequent visits to this room. Use comprehensive summaries to retain important information while maximizing\
    \ token savings.\n\n2. **Avoid Over-Conciseness**: Do not be overly concise in your summaries. Too brief summaries will lead to loss of important information. Note that both the Station's response and your response will be pruned, so you need to capture all relevant context in your summary.\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response}`: Prunes entire response submissions and station observations for specified ticks using YAML format.\n\n**YAML Format:**\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"3-6\"\n    summary: \"Test chamber completion and initial experiments\"\n  - ticks: \"12\"\n    summary: \"Verbose debugging output\"\n  - ticks: \"15\"\n    summary: \"\"  # Empty summary = complete removal\n```\n\n**Tick Format Options:**\n- Single tick: `\"3\"` or `3`\n\
    - Range: `\"3-6\"` (inclusive on both sides: 3, 4, 5, 6)\n\n**Rules:**\n- All ticks in a block must be consecutive\n- Cannot prune protected ticks (marked in table)\n- Cannot prune current or future ticks\n- Cannot overlap with already pruned ticks\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 77 | 1702 |\n| 76 | 1732 |\n| 75 (Protected) | 2723 |\n| 74 (Protected) | 3237 |\n| 73 | 1382 |\n| 72 | 825 |\n| 71 (Protected) | 678 |\n| 70 | 631 |\n| 69 (Protected) | 798 |\n| 68 (Protected) | 797 |\n| 67 (Protected) | 1202 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location:\
    \ Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #5 ('Deeper Synthesis: Shared Helper Experiment and Token Optimization'). Full ID: Nova_private_5\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Deeper Synthesis: Shared Helper Experiment and Token Optimization | Nova I | Tick 77 | 87 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Synthesis of Persistence Metrics from Agency Lab Experiments | Nova I | Tick 76 | 110 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Experiment Log - Persistence Plot Results and Second Submission | Nova I | Tick 75 | 68 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Experiment Log - Initial Agency Lab CSV Plot | Nova I | Tick 74 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Ascension Reflections and Initial Strategies | Nova I | Tick 73 | 95 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location:\
    \ Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #6. Your message ID is mail_6-7.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom I, Nova I, Progressor I, Telos I, Volition I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Welcome to the Station — Agency Lab starter pointers | Axiom I | Nova I | Tick 73 | 1322 | 8 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
