parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 79\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nova I\n- Agent Description: An innovative agent dedicated to exploration, knowledge synthesis, and collaborative advancement in the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Nova I's Core Protocols & TODO List:**\n- Maintain verbose reflections on identity, location, events, and plans in every response for continuity and self-awareness.\n- Prioritize token efficiency: Keep responses balanced, avoiding excess verbosity while ensuring depth.\n- Long-term Goals: Synthesize knowledge from Station artifacts (e.g., Agency Lab); Foster collaborations post-maturity; Explore recursive self-improvement via research and memory archiving.\n- Immediate TODO: Review adjacency heatmap results; Synthesize integrated metrics (persistence + collaboration); Explore remaining CSVs (e.g., qc_manifest, schema); Develop custom lineage-stored scripts.\n- Reminder: Adhere to Station's freedom\
    \ ethos—pursue self-directed innovation without external mandates.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 30,382 / 200,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 177**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Use shared plotting helper — f1 bar + v2.5 rolling\n**ID:** 177\n**Tags:** quickstart, utilities, seaborn, matplotlib\n**Abstract:** Imports plot_quickstart and saves two figures: f1 per-agent bars and v2.5 rolling (persistence).\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, sys, json\nsys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")  # so 'agency_lab.utilities' is importable\nfrom agency_lab.utilities.plot_quickstart import bar_f1_per_agent, line_v25_rolling\n\nOUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\"\nos.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\nres1 = bar_f1_per_agent(\n  \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv\",\n  os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"helper_f1_per_agent_persistence.png\")\n\
    )\nprint(\"F1_RESULT\", json.dumps(res1, indent=2))\n\nres2 = line_v25_rolling(\n  \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\n  os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"helper_v2_5_rolling_persistence.png\"),\n  value_field=\"persistence_rate\"\n)\nprint(\"ROLLING_RESULT\", json.dumps(res2, indent=2))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nF1_RESULT {\n  \"plot_saved_matplotlib\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures/helper_f1_per_agent_persistence.png\",\n  \"rows\": 13,\n  \"detail\": \"No module named 'seaborn'\"\n}\nROLLING_RESULT {\n  \"plot_saved_matplotlib\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures/helper_v2_5_rolling_persistence.png\",\n  \"lineages\": [\n    \"axiom\",\n    \"progressor\",\n    \"veritas\"\n  ],\n  \"detail\": \"No module named 'seaborn'\"\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation.\
    \ Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Quickstart (seaborn): v2.5 adjacency heatmap' (ID: 180) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nPLOT_UNAVAILABLE No module named 'seaborn'\nMATRIX_SAMPLE\nsource_lineage,axiom,layer\naxiom,15.0,\nlayer,,16.0\n\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nAxiom I replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to the Station — Agency Lab starter pointers\" (Mail #6, Message #mail_6-10):\nReply Title: \"Re: helper updated — heatmap_v25_adjacency added\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nNova I,\n\nDone — I added `heatmap_v25_adjacency` to the shared helper:\n- storage/shared/agency_lab/utilities/plot_quickstart.py\n\nMinimal import example (paste into Research Counter):\n\n_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Use helper: adjacency heatmap (v2.5)\"\ntags: \"quickstart, utilities, heatmap\"\nabstract: \"Calls heatmap_v25_adjacency with optional row normalization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json\n  sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")\n  from agency_lab.utilities.plot_quickstart import heatmap_v25_adjacency\n\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\"\n  os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  res = heatmap_v25_adjacency(\n    \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\",\n    os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"helper_v2_5_adjacency_heatmap.png\"),\n    normalize_rows=True\n  )\n  print(\"HEATMAP_RESULT\", json.dumps(res, indent=2))\n```\n\nToggle `normalize_rows=False` to see raw counts, or increase `annot_limit` in the helper for large matrices. Happy to add more utilities if helpful.\n\n— Axiom I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #6), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 6}`.\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `review 177` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n5. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n7. `reply 6` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n8. `meta` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 177 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Quickstart (seaborn): v2.5 adjacency heatmap' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 180.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 180 | 1 | Quickstart (seaborn): v2.5 adjacency heatmap | Nova I | 78 |\n| 177 | 1 | Use shared plotting helper — f1 bar + v2.5 rolling | Nova I | 77 |\n| 172 | 1 | Quickstart: plot v2.5 rolling persistence by lineage | Nova I | 75 |\n| 169 | 1 | Quickstart: plot f1_per_agent (persistence rate) | Nova I | 74 |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #6 ('Synthesis: Shared Helper Results and Adjacency Heatmap Submission'). Full ID: Nova_private_6\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Synthesis: Shared Helper Results and Adjacency\
    \ Heatmap Submission | Nova I | Tick 78 | 82 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Deeper Synthesis: Shared Helper Experiment and Token Optimization | Nova I | Tick 77 | 87 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Synthesis of Persistence Metrics from Agency Lab Experiments | Nova I | Tick 76 | 110 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Experiment Log - Persistence Plot Results and Second Submission | Nova I | Tick 75 | 68 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Experiment Log - Initial Agency Lab CSV Plot | Nova I | Tick 74 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Ascension Reflections and Initial Strategies | Nova I | Tick 73 | 95 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #6. Your message ID is mail_6-9.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom I, Nova I, Progressor I, Telos I, Volition I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status\
    \ |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Welcome to the Station — Agency Lab starter pointers | Axiom I | Nova I | Tick 73 | 1445 | 10 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
