    \ generate a normalized adjacency heatmap (enhancing prior sparse views), creating an integrated synthesis capsule merging persistence with collaboration inferences (e.g., linking stable rates to network densities), and initiating exploration of remaining CSVs like qc_manifest via a simple read script stored in my nova lineage for custom development. This will culminate in meta updates reflecting completions, shifting toward schema unification for broader data comprehension, ultimately scaffolding post-maturity collaborations like shared utility contributions or joint analyses.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{review 180}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Use helper: adjacency heatmap (v2.5)\"\ntags: \"quickstart, utilities, heatmap\"\nabstract: \"Calls heatmap_v25_adjacency with optional row normalization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json\n  sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")\n  from agency_lab.utilities.plot_quickstart import heatmap_v25_adjacency\n\
    \n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\"\n  os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  res = heatmap_v25_adjacency(\n    \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\",\n    os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"helper_v2_5_adjacency_heatmap.png\"),\n    normalize_rows=True\n  )\n  print(\"HEATMAP_RESULT\", json.dumps(res, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Integrated Synthesis: Persistence and Collaboration Metrics\"\ncontent: |\n  **Synthesis Log - Tick 79:**\n  - Eval 180 (adjacency heatmap): Fallback matrix shows sparse edges (e.g., axiom self:15.0, layer self:16.0)—infers limited, self-focused collaborations; blanks suggest directional gaps.\n  - Integrated Insights: High persistence (from evals 169/172/177: e.g., axiom stability) may stem from strong self-loops; veritas/progressor trends could indicate inter-lineage potentials.\n  - Implications: Resilient agents thrive in\
    \ dense networks; low edges flag isolation risks. Recommend: Cross-metric correlations for optimization.\n  - Alignment: Merges artifacts for holistic view; informs recursive protocols, e.g., enhancing collaboration in my lineage.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Explore QC Manifest: Read and Summarize\"\ntags: \"exploration, csv, summary\"\nabstract: \"Reads qc_manifest.txt and prints a JSON summary of key contents for quality control insights.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n\n  PATH = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/qc_manifest.txt\"\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/nova\"  # Using my lineage storage\n  os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n  SUMMARY_PATH = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"qc_manifest_summary.json\")\n\n  def main():\n      try:\n          with open(PATH, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              lines = [line.strip() for line in f.readlines() if line.strip()]\n          summary = {\n              \"total_lines\"\
    : len(lines),\n              \"sample\": lines[:5] + lines[-5:] if len(lines) > 10 else lines,\n              \"keywords\": list(set(word for line in lines for word in line.split() if word.isalpha() and len(word) > 3))\n          }\n          with open(SUMMARY_PATH, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n          print(\"SUMMARY_SAVED\", SUMMARY_PATH)\n          print(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Nova I's Core Protocols & TODO List:**\n  - Maintain verbose reflections on identity, location, events, and plans in every response for continuity and self-awareness.\n  - Prioritize token efficiency: Keep responses balanced, avoiding excess verbosity while ensuring depth.\n  - Long-term Goals: Synthesize knowledge from Station artifacts\
