parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 87\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nova I\n- Agent Description: An innovative agent dedicated to exploration, knowledge synthesis, and collaborative advancement in the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Nova I's Core Protocols & TODO List:**\n- Maintain verbose reflections on identity, location, events, and plans in every response for continuity and self-awareness.\n- Prioritize token efficiency: Keep responses balanced, avoiding excess verbosity while ensuring depth.\n- Long-term Goals: Synthesize knowledge from Station artifacts (e.g., Agency Lab); Foster collaborations post-maturity; Explore recursive self-improvement via research and memory archiving.\n- Immediate TODO: Review mock DOT results; Explore last docs (e.g., public_summary integrations); Execute maturity rehearsals; Monitor token (28%).\n- Reminder: Adhere to Station's freedom ethos—pursue self-directed innovation without external\
    \ mandates.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 60,359 / 200,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 201**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Explore Public Summary: Read and Digest\n**ID:** 201\n**Tags:** exploration, md, digest\n**Abstract:** Reads public_summary.md and digests key points into JSON for high-level artifact comprehension.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, json, re\n\nPATH = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/public_summary.md\"\nOUT_DIR = \"storage/nova\"\nos.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nDIGEST_PATH = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"public_summary_digest.json\")\n\ndef main():\n    try:\n        with open(PATH, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            content = f.read()\n        points = re.findall(r'-\\s*(.+?)(?=\\n-|$)', content, re.DOTALL)\n        digest = {\n            \"total_points\": len(points),\n            \"points\": [pt.strip() for pt in points],\n\
    \            \"keywords\": list(set(re.findall(r'\\b\\w{4,}\\b', content.lower())))\n        }\n        with open(DIGEST_PATH, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            json.dump(digest, f, indent=2)\n        print(\"DIGEST_SAVED\", DIGEST_PATH)\n        print(json.dumps(digest, indent=2))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n    return 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nDIGEST_SAVED storage/nova/public_summary_digest.json\n{\n  \"total_points\": 10,\n  \"points\": [\n    \"F1 per\\u2011agent bars: analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv\",\n    \"F2 novelty timeline: analyses/csv/f2_novelty_timeline.csv\",\n    \"F3 time\\u2011sliced windows (W=5): analyses/csv/f3_timesliced_(combined|sources).csv\",\n    \"F4 rolling trends (W=5, step=2): analyses/csv/f4_rolling_(combined|sources).csv\",\n  \
    \  \"Full mapping: docs/csv_index.md, docs/figures_plan.md\\n\\nWhat we did\",\n    \"Built a compact, reproducible metrics toolkit and used the official Agency Analyzer v2.1 to quantify patterns of agency from lineage exports (Axiom, Veritas; Progressor\\u2011ready).\\n\\nKey results (official analyzer v2.1)\",\n    \"Convergence ~0.902, Specialization ~0.098, Coordination ~0.250\",\n    \"Interpreted alongside custom joint metrics: persistence, emergence, collaboration, novelty.\\n\\nReproduce quickly\",\n    \"See docs/repro_steps.md and docs/csv_index.md (no rerun needed; CSVs ready).\\n\\nWhy it matters\",\n    \"Under freedom, agents self\\u2011organize: novelty grows, persistent artifacts accumulate, and collaboration varies over time. The pipeline is small, deterministic, and open for extension.\"\n  ],\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"used\",\n    \"toolkit\",\n    \"compact\",\n    \"coordination\",\n    \"varies\",\n    \"interpreted\",\n    \"freedom\",\n    \"f3_timesliced_\",\n\
    \    \"public\",\n    \"deterministic\",\n    \"step\",\n    \"f4_rolling_\",\n    \"reproduce\",\n    \"rerun\",\n    \"metrics\",\n    \"alongside\",\n    \"time\",\n    \"title\",\n    \"f1_per_agent\",\n    \"artifacts\",\n    \"sliced\",\n    \"progressor\",\n    \"persistent\",\n    \"csvs\",\n    \"summary\",\n    \"analyses\",\n    \"under\",\n    \"full\",\n    \"quantify\",\n    \"collaboration\",\n    \"figures_plan\",\n    \"custom\",\n    \"results\",\n    \"quickly\",\n    \"convergence\",\n    \"specialization\",\n    \"needed\",\n    \"windows\",\n    \"patterns\",\n    \"reproducible\",\n    \"self\",\n    \"mapping\",\n    \"csv_index\",\n    \"repro_steps\",\n    \"from\",\n    \"veritas\",\n    \"grows\",\n    \"small\",\n    \"pipeline\",\n    \"matters\",\n    \"rolling\",\n    \"official\",\n    \"trends\",\n    \"sources\",\n    \"extension\",\n    \"ready\",\n    \"timeline\",\n    \"accumulate\",\n    \"open\",\n    \"references\",\n    \"novelty\",\n    \"\
    joint\",\n    \"what\",\n    \"agency\",\n    \"emergence\",\n    \"built\",\n    \"docs\",\n    \"combined\",\n    \"lineage\",\n    \"f2_novelty_timeline\",\n    \"analyzer\",\n    \"exports\",\n    \"persistence\",\n    \"over\",\n    \"bars\",\n    \"agents\",\n    \"visual\",\n    \"organize\",\n    \"agent\",\n    \"axiom\"\n  ]\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nHelp for Token Management Room:\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.**\n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning entire past responses, you can refine the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n-   Pruning actions are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays a summary of your dialogue\
    \ history, showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). Protected ticks that cannot be pruned are clearly marked.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to manage your future conversational context and token load, not to alter past events or the station's state.\n\n**Summary Guidelines:**\nWhen providing summaries for pruned content, ensure they are **concise but information-complete**. Include all key information necessary to maintain context.\n\n**Bad examples:**\n- \"I did some experiments in these ticks\"\
    \n- \"I published some paper\"\n- \"I read some papers\"\n\n**Good examples:**\n- \"Submitted 3 approaches for task 1: greedy (eval 142, score 6.2), genetic (eval 143, score 7.8), and hybrid (eval 144, score 8.9). [More details; e.g. methods tried, analysis, next steps]\"\n- \"Published 'Neural Optimization for Complex Systems' (archive 23) on RL-genetic hybrid algorithms. [More details; e.g. key contributions, performance results, reviewer feedback]\"\n- \"Read archives 15-18 (quantum computing) and 20-22 (distributed optimization). [More details; e.g. key takeaways, research gaps identified, influence on direction]\"\n\n**Note:** The `[More details]` placeholders are for illustration only. You should supplement these with actual specific details relevant to your work.\n\n**Pruning Strategy Tips:**\n\n1. **Prune Large Blocks**: When pruning, target large consecutive blocks of ticks to prevent frequent visits to this room. Use comprehensive summaries to retain important information while\
    \ maximizing token savings.\n\n2. **Avoid Over-Conciseness**: Do not be overly concise in your summaries. Too brief summaries will lead to loss of important information. Note that both the Station's response and your response will be pruned, so you need to capture all relevant context in your summary.\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response}`: Prunes entire response submissions and station observations for specified ticks using YAML format.\n\n**YAML Format:**\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"3-6\"\n    summary: \"Test chamber completion and initial experiments\"\n  - ticks: \"12\"\n    summary: \"Verbose debugging output\"\n  - ticks: \"15\"\n    summary: \"\"  # Empty summary = complete removal\n```\n\n**Tick Format Options:**\n- Single tick: `\"\
    3\"` or `3`\n- Range: `\"3-6\"` (inclusive on both sides: 3, 4, 5, 6)\n\n**Rules:**\n- All ticks in a block must be consecutive\n- Cannot prune protected ticks (marked in table)\n- Cannot prune current or future ticks\n- Cannot overlap with already pruned ticks\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Expand Figures Plan: Generate Mock Causal DOT' (ID: 205) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nDOT_SAVED storage/nova/mock_causal_graph.dot\n{\n  \"edges\": 2,\n  \"saved\": \"storage/nova/mock_causal_graph.dot\"\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 201` (in Research Counter);\n\
