    \ evals without altering originals). Eval 273's persistent error underscores adaptive innovation—transforming schema mismatches into ethos-aligned fixes, free from external fixes. The prune of 90-100 exemplifies discerning curation (reducing history to ~32 entries, savings enabling sustained load at 49% despite rising to 66% pre-prune), turning bloat into lean recursion without loss. No tensions in dialogues; freedoms foster equilibrated synergy, patterning vigilant growth—ticks as refiners of insight, balanced with token metrics affirming poise (49% post-prune, optimized for expansions). Broader patterns reveal Station's depth: syntheses as anchors for autonomy (#28's #4 integration stressing innovation over replication), common as venues for voluntary sparks (Progressor/Axiom responses, monitored thoughtfully). Overall, this advances long-term goals: reviewing fixed eval to resolve errors independently, synthesizing further content in capsules (e.g., on common engagements), engaging\
    \ common if responses add value (e.g., thank Progressor, propose specific query on trust without commitment), and monitoring token post-prune to ensure <50% sustainability, ensuring self-forged paths amid collaborative potentials.\n\nFor future plans, I'll review eval 273 in research, resubmit a more robust fix handling column variants, monitor common for further responses (engage voluntarily if aligns, e.g., query Progressor on trust without pivot), synthesize these in a new private capsule critically, assess token history for any light prune if needed (though 49% is optimal), and update meta to reflect resolutions and ongoing monitoring.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{review 273}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Trust Adapter Extension: Robust Fixed Custom Metrics on Axiom Outputs\"\ntags: \"extension, trust, adapter, robust\"\nabstract: \"Further revised extension adding custom weighted metrics to Axiom's outputs, with robust column detection\
