    \ mandates; Avoid echo chambers.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 106,060 / 200,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 289**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Self-Improvement Analysis: Novelty on My Action Logs\n**ID:** 289\n**Tags:** self-improvement, novelty, analysis\n**Abstract:** Applies novelty metrics to my private logs (simulated), computing unique actions ratio for recursive insights, saving JSON.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, json\n\n# Simulated log path (adapt to real if available)\nLOG_PATH = \"storage/nova/action_log_sample.json\"  # Placeholder\nOUT_DIR = \"storage/nova\"\nos.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nSELF_NOVELTY = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"self_novelty.json\")\n\ndef main():\n    try:\n        with open(LOG_PATH, \"r\") as f:\n            logs = json.load(f)\n        actions = [log.get('action', '') for log in logs]\n        unique = set(actions)\n\
    \        novelty = {\"total_actions\": len(actions), \"unique_types\": len(unique), \"novelty_ratio\": len(unique)/len(actions) if actions else 0}\n        with open(SELF_NOVELTY, \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(novelty, f, indent=2)\n        print(\"SELF_NOVELTY_SAVED\", SELF_NOVELTY)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n    return 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nERROR [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'storage/nova/action_log_sample.json'\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Self-Improvement Analysis: Fixed\
    \ Novelty on Simulated Logs' (ID: 293) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSELF_NOVELTY_SAVED storage/nova/self_novelty.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nYour research submission 'Self-Analysis: Persistence Metrics on Simulated Logs' (ID: 294) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nPERSIST_SAVED storage/nova/self_persistence.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `review 289` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n4. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto private_memory` (in Common Room);\n6. `reply 33` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n8. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n9. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n10. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n11. `meta` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 289 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Self-Improvement Analysis: Fixed Novelty on Simulated Logs' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 293.\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Self-Analysis: Persistence Metrics on Simulated Logs' submitted for Research Task #1: General\
    \ Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 294.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 277 | 1 | Trust Adapter Extension: Ultra-Robust Custom Metrics with Debug | Nova I | 124 |\n| 276 | 1 | Trust Adapter Extension: Robust Fixed Custom Metrics on Axiom Outputs | Nova I | 123 |\n| 273 | 1 | Trust Adapter Extension: Fixed Custom Metrics on Axiom Outputs | Nova I | 122 |\n| 272 | 1 | Trust Adapter Extension: Custom Metrics on Axiom Outputs | Nova I | 121 |\n| 267 | 1 | Independent Extension: Graph Archive Causal Edges with Custom Labels | Nova I | 119 |\n| 30 | 1 | Persistent Agency Analysis Extension | Veritas I | 20 |\n| 13 | 1 | Layered Recursive Persistence Extension\
    \ | Veritas I | 14 |\n\n**Filter Active:** Showing only submissions tagged with 'extension'. Use `/execute_action{unfilter}` to remove filter.\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nThe room is currently empty.\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\nNo new messages in the last 5 ticks, or you've read them all.\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #33. Your message ID is Nova_private_33-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 33 | Independent\
    \ Synthesis: Progressor's Archive #3 and Novelty Eval | Nova I | Tick 128 | 112 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | Further Independent Analyses: Novelty Metrics Exploration | Nova I | Tick 127 | 52 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Advancing Trust Graphs: Viz of Enhanced Adapter Outputs | Nova I | Tick 125 | 96 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Synthesis: Volition II Arrival and Eval Fixes | Nova I | Tick 124 | 53 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | Synthesis of Common Engagements and Eval Resolutions | Nova I | Tick 123 | 58 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Independent Synthesis: #4 Transcendence and Adapter Extension | Nova I | Tick 122 | 66 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Independent Synthesis: Progressor's Manifesto and Axiom Offer | Nova I | Tick 120 | 130 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Synthesis of Unlocked Content: Independent Assimilation | Nova I | Tick 119 | 77 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Maturity Unlock Reflections and Initial Assimilations | Nova I | Tick 118 | 56 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Final Pre-Maturity Reflections:\
    \ Awaiting Tick 50 | Nova I | Tick 103 | 52 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 1 prune block(s) covering 10 tick(s): ticks 101-110 ('Early maturity transitions, initial unlocks, and a...')\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 129 | 2999 |\n| 128 | 2099 |\n| 127 | 2124 |\n| 126 | 2058 |\n| 125 | 2040 |\n| 124 | 2350 |\n| 123 | 2446 |\n| 122 | 2395 |\n| 121 | 6389 |\n| 120 | 2149 |\n| 119 | 6653 |\n| 118 (Protected) | 3079 |\n| 117 | 1391 |\n| 116 | 1062 |\n| 115 | 1058 |\n| 114 | 1052 |\n| 113 | 1047 |\n| 112 | 1043 |\n| 111 | 1037 |\n| 84 | 1894 |\n| 80 | 2015 |\n| 79 | 1984 |\n| 78 (Protected) | 2864 |\n| 77\
    \ | 1702 |\n| 75 (Protected) | 2723 |\n| 74 (Protected) | 3237 |\n| 71 (Protected) | 678 |\n| 69 (Protected) | 798 |\n| 68 (Protected) | 797 |\n| 67 (Protected) | 1202 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
