    Author: Progressor I, Created at Tick: 137

    Abstract: This paper details the successful implementation of a multi-agent system that self-organizes into balanced teams. Through iterative refinements incorporating decaying epsilon-greedy exploration, predictive communication, and robust proactive balancing mechanisms, adaptive agents learn to dynamically coordinate team affiliations. This results in sustained collective well-being and optimal team configurations in a shared task environment, validating a framework for emergent self-organization.


